237
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:24,808
row or, you know, on a down-moving market if they're up above the red bars.

238
00:12:24,810 --> 00:12:27,201
Where your point of entry is, it's

239
00:12:27,201 --> 00:12:29,934
somewhere, you know, between these two points of

240
00:12:29,934 --> 00:12:33,009
controls, between the third bar and the second bar.

241
00:12:34,610 --> 00:12:37,370
You want to get a little bit of a pullback for a better entry.

242
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:40,530
There's going to be times where it just continues on and you miss your entry.

243
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:42,007
But, you know, I prefer

244
00:12:42,007 --> 00:12:44,371
to have a little bit of wiggle room

245
00:12:44,371 --> 00:12:48,508
by, you know, getting a better entry rather than just paying in the market.

246
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:53,590
So a continuation pattern allows you to find an entry point in an existing trend.

247
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:57,970
Trends are where the big money is made in trading, so it's your benefit to jump in in a trend.

248
00:12:57,970 --> 00:13:03,310
And some traders base their entire trading program on just jumping along for the ride.

249
00:13:03,490 --> 00:13:06,750
So it'll benefit you to have a few continuation patterns and setups to look for.

250
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:09,272
You know, I mean, like

251
00:13:09,272 --> 00:13:11,263
I said, you know, some of these

252
00:13:11,263 --> 00:13:14,960
hedge funds and CTAs that have been around for 20, 30 years are trend followers.

253
00:13:16,350 --> 00:13:19,910
You know, they're not trying to pick tops and bottoms.

254
00:13:20,330 --> 00:13:25,590
They just want to identify when a trend is occurring and ride it for as long as they can.

255
00:13:25,590 --> 00:13:32,210
And, you know, these guys, that's why they trade, you know, 50, 60 different markets around the world.

256
00:13:32,350 --> 00:13:34,950
They're looking for the six or seven or eight markets

257
00:13:34,950 --> 00:13:36,510
a year that have the monster

258
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:39,110
trends where they're going to make up all their money.

259
00:13:39,530 --> 00:13:40,930
That's why, you know, they're

260
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:42,890
willing to take a bunch of small

261
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:45,690
losses, but their winners is going to be quite big.

262
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:53,080
So when a trend is underway and there's a pattern telling you to buy, you buy.

263
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:59,080
Just as if the market is telling you to sell, you sell, especially in a trend.

264
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,418
You know, you want to

265
00:14:00,418 --> 00:14:02,011
ride the trend because, you know, when

266
00:14:02,011 --> 00:14:03,832
the market moves from a low to a

267
00:14:03,832 --> 00:14:07,019
high and you're not in on it, you know, you feel like an idiot.

268
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:11,640
But, you know, I mean, you still need a reason to get into the trade.

269
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,440
All right, so let's take a look at a chart.

270
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,020
Here you have a bond chart.

271
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:19,080
We came into the low at 11.45.

272
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:24,540
You have the single print. Then, you know, 30 minutes later, you have another single print.

273
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:29,720
So now you're sort of convinced yourself that the trend is up, that we're starting to move away.

274
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,800
Where's your continuation pattern?

275
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:34,500
If you come back down to the same level, it holds.

276
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:36,219
Then you're starting to see,

277
00:14:36,219 --> 00:14:38,345
you know, as you're moving up, you're

278
00:14:38,345 --> 00:14:40,775
starting to see confirmation with single print, single

279
00:14:40,775 --> 00:14:42,598
print, and the market moves higher.

280
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:50,440
This one's a little bit more messy, but nevertheless, I'll talk about it.

281
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:56,280
We sort of peaked up here at 10.18 in the bonds and start coming down.

282
00:14:56,860 --> 00:15:02,980
You have a ratio here of 0.53, and the market proceeds to go sideways.

283
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,951
Now, you know,

284
00:15:04,951 --> 00:15:07,263
I know the high is here, and

285
00:15:07,263 --> 00:15:09,575
what's happening is you're starting to get

286
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:12,218
a couple ratios here, a couple ratios here.

287
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:17,840
But it's kind of hard to really get a good gauge on which way the market's going to go.

288
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:20,960
So what I'm looking at is where the points of controls are.

289
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:24,640
Now, I know the points of control here, here, here.

290
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:29,260
I had talked about earlier, you know, using point of controls as support or resistance.

291
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,544
So, in this case, I'm

292
00:15:30,544 --> 00:15:32,342
using, I think, the market is in

293
00:15:32,342 --> 00:15:34,397
a downtrend, because, you know, I know we

294
00:15:34,397 --> 00:15:37,479
have a high here, and I see this ratio of bounds low.

295
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,503
Even though you have a single

296
00:15:40,503 --> 00:15:42,326
print here, a large print here,

297
00:15:42,326 --> 00:15:44,756
but you have opposing single prints just on

298
00:15:44,756 --> 00:15:46,579
the other side of these two.

299
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:52,200
But what's interesting is you have the points of controls all lining up right here, you know.

300
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:58,040
So now, I'm not too concerned about these, you know, because this one still has a negative delta.

301
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,760
This one has a small positive delta.

302
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:05,040
You know, if I'm expecting the market to really move higher, I want to see a strong positive delta.

303
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:10,880
So, you know, I'm able to take this ratio, this ratio, this ratio more seriously than these two.

304
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,940
In fact, I got the points of controls here.

305
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:17,120
You know, I'm still looking for a downtrend. I'm still looking for the market to move lower.

306
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:23,440
Then I'm seeing a few more confirmation ratios here, you know, a ratio of bounds low and a single print.

307
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:26,200
You know, so it's telling me, you know, the move should be lower.

308
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:35,550
Again, this is the bond, and, you know, you hit the high, and we start working our way down.

309
00:16:35,650 --> 00:16:39,850
You're seeing the single prints here with nice ratios, 77 to 82.

310
00:16:41,590 --> 00:16:46,470
And, you know, you're thinking already the trend is, you know, lower.

311
00:16:47,070 --> 00:16:48,590
You know, maybe you're not convinced yet.

312
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,670
You know, you want a little bit extra,

313
00:16:50,670 --> 00:16:52,750
but, you know, you're seeing the selling imbalances,

314
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:54,830
selling imbalances, selling imbalances, selling imbalances, selling imbalances.

315
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:57,790
You know, if you're still not convinced, this bar here

316
00:16:57,790 --> 00:16:59,242
has got a very strong negative

317
00:16:59,242 --> 00:17:02,388
delta, and then immediately it's followed by a bar with a single print.

318
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:04,988
So, it's telling you, you know, you should

319
00:17:04,988 --> 00:17:07,286
have been alert way up here, but, you

320
00:17:07,286 --> 00:17:11,308
know, we're in the trend already, so you're looking for a sign of continuation.

321
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:14,045
You're seeing a delta very strong.

322
00:17:14,045 --> 00:17:16,060
You're seeing a lot of selling

323
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:18,075
imbalances. You're seeing the single print

324
00:17:18,075 --> 00:17:21,769
to help confirm the ratio, sorry, help confirm the move lower.

325
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:28,060
Okay. Now, this is an E-mini chart.

326
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:32,040
Now, we've come down into our low here. We've got a buying imbalance right on the low.

327
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:34,480
Okay. Maybe you're not yet convinced that this is the low.

328
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:37,140
You know, you want to see the trend start to happen before getting in.

329
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:42,660
And, boom, you get this other ratio bounce low here indicating some stopping volume.

330
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:47,580
And, you're getting another buying imbalance, you know, and the market worked its way back up.

331
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:55,180
Okay. S&P's, again, we're working our way lower.

332
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:59,441
You know, we've got a ratio bounce low,

333
00:17:59,441 --> 00:18:01,047
some heavy volume here. We've got

334
00:18:01,047 --> 00:18:04,259
a single print. You get a pullback up to the single print.

335
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,600
Okay. You know you're working your way lower.

336
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,756
You get a pullback.

337
00:18:07,756 --> 00:18:09,909
You know, well, you know, I'm not sure

338
00:18:09,909 --> 00:18:13,139
if this is a pullback or we're just going to go higher.

339
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,080
So, you want to have some extra confirmation.

340
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:15,840
Now, you have it.

341
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,140
You have the selling imbalance and the market sells off.

342
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:26,260
This by itself where we trace back up to the single print for me is normally a good trade.

343
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:31,120
I like it when the market circles back up to a single print, you know, to get short.

344
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:35,196
You know, then when I see a selling

345
00:18:35,196 --> 00:18:38,080
imbalance, you know, then it tells me

346
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:42,200
to hold on to the trade a bit longer. Okay.

347
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,100
So, you know, we're working our way up.

348
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,800
Nice, you know, ratios here.

349
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,460
Your blueprints is telling you we're in a trend already.

350
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,820
You know, you really should have been looking to get long in here.

351
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,927
You know, say you missed it. You're looking

352
00:18:53,927 --> 00:18:57,299
for another reason to get long that the trend is going to keep continuing.

353
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,020
And what do you have?

354
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:00,400
You've got buying imbalance here.

355
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:02,352
You know, I'm usually not a big person

356
00:19:02,352 --> 00:19:03,885
to get long in a buying imbalance.

357
00:19:03,885 --> 00:19:05,856
But, you know what? This is one of those

358
00:19:05,856 --> 00:19:10,237
cases where if you have a tight stop, you know, I usually like to get long in a buying imbalance.

359
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:12,820
I'd prefer to get a little bit lower, though.

360
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:14,861
So, you know, but if you have a

361
00:19:14,861 --> 00:19:16,647
tight stop, you can manage it and,

362
00:19:16,647 --> 00:19:21,239
you know, it's going to give you a chance to get back in on the move back up.

363
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:28,740
Like I said, you have this high here with the ratio of a single print sort of standing in your way.

364
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:34,240
But, you know what? If you're able to get in somewhere down here, you know, your risk is relatively low.

365
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,860
Because usually I like to see a pull back up to this level.

366
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,886
So, you know, if you're going to get

367
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:41,899
a pull back up to that level, you may have a chance to get past it.

368
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:44,569
You know, sometimes it's hard to sell a

369
00:19:44,569 --> 00:19:46,782
high just off of a single print

370
00:19:46,782 --> 00:19:48,679
and a ratio and negative delta.

371
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:52,460
But, you know, there are times when it

372
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,260
doesn't work. And, you know, if you're

373
00:19:55,260 --> 00:20:00,060
looking for a continuation of a trend, then it's going to happen.

374
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:05,980
That one made no sense. Okay.

375
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:06,820
Now, what do you have here?

376
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:07,720
You've got an E-mini chart.

377
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:09,040
Markets coming down, down, down.

378
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:11,080
You've got a couple of selling imbalances right in a row.

379
00:20:11,740 --> 00:20:15,440
Now, this is, I like this, where you get two selling imbalances split over two bars.

380
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:20,580
You get the pull back up here in a single print and then the market sells off.

381
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:26,680
You know, when you're seeing selling imbalances, you know, going into a low, you might want to be careful.

382
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:29,179
But if you get a pull back in there, you know, it's

383
00:20:29,179 --> 00:20:32,719
telling you that these most likely are going to hold and the market's going to continue lower.

384
00:20:35,270 --> 00:20:37,610
You know, again, we're sort of coming off our high up here.

385
00:20:37,650 --> 00:20:38,670
We've got a selling imbalance.

386
00:20:39,550 --> 00:20:43,890
Then you're seeing the confirmation with the ratios, the blue numbers, as the market's moving lower.

387
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:50,360
So this is the end of Lesson 17, Continuation Setups.

388
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:54,500
In the next lesson, I'll explain how to integrate order flow with

389
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:57,580
your traditional technical analysis to enhance your current ways of trading.

390
00:20:57,580 --> 00:21:01,538
I mean, you know, I didn't spend much time under

391
00:21:01,538 --> 00:21:04,704
Continuation Setups because it should be pretty easy,

392
00:21:04,704 --> 00:21:07,079
I think, for you to spot.

393
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,540
You know, I gave you a few setups that I like to look for.

394
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:15,600
But in general, you're still looking for the same things that you're looking for around reversals.

395
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:19,116
You know, with Continuations, it's generally because you missed the

396
00:21:19,116 --> 00:21:24,039
reversal sign and you're getting in just a little bit late on the Continuation.

397
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:29,960
But, I mean, you should always be looking for, you know, any setups where they're occurring.

398
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:32,900
Just take them into context with where the market is.

399
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:37,660
You know, if the market is trending, it's okay to take the setups.

400
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:42,140
If the market is going sideways, you know, I'm a bit hesitant to take setups.

401
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:48,580
You know, I said I want a market to be moving, not basically spinning its wheels.

402
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:53,080
You know, when a market's moving is when you're going to have the opportunity to make money.

403
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,820
So the important thing is, you know, just be able to determine when the market is moving.

404
00:21:57,180 --> 00:21:58,900
And if you're seeing a setup, take it.

405
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:02,560
If the market is not moving and you see a setup, be hesitant.

406
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:06,740
So thank you. That's the end of Lesson 17.

